# Post-Implementation Checkpoint

## Required Context
After completing implementation, verify the following context elements:

1. Test Status
   - All tests for the sub-feature are passing
   - No regressions in other tests
   - Test coverage is adequate

2. Implementation Status
   - All requirements for the sub-feature are implemented
   - Code quality meets standards
   - Implementation file is updated with [test-passing] status
   - Active working context is updated to reflect completion

3. Next Steps
   - Next sub-feature is identified (if applicable)
   - If all sub-features are complete, feature status needs updating
   - Test requirements for next sub-feature are defined (if applicable)

## Verification Steps
- [ ] Run all tests to confirm they pass
- [ ] Validate implementation against requirements
- [ ] Update implementation file with current status
- [ ] Update active-working-feature-context.mdc
- [ ] Identify next steps in the implementation process

## Context Updates
After successful implementation:
1. Update the implementation file to mark sub-feature as [test-passing]
2. Update active-working-feature-context.mdc with implementation details
3. If all sub-features are complete, update core-mechanics.mdc to mark feature as [done]
4. Document the implementation in the progress history

## Expected Output
After completing this checkpoint, you should have:
- Passing tests for the implemented sub-feature
- Updated implementation file reflecting [test-passing] status
- Updated active working context with implementation details
- Clear next steps for continuing development
- If feature is complete, updated core-mechanics.mdc 